
# Part E - Project Application

## E1 - Project Connection

My final project is Campus Cafeteria Order Management.

The program manages cafeteria orders, including delivery orders.

## E2 - Temporary View

The temporary view contains only active DELIVERY orders.

An active order has the status PENDING or IN_PROGRESS.

The program stores pointers to the original orders instead of copying the records.

## E3 - Sorting Criteria

The delivery report can be sorted using these fields:

1. Building in alphabetical order.
2. Priority from highest to lowest.
3. Order ID from lowest to highest.

These fields help organize the delivery report without changing the original order records.

## E4 - Original Data

The original orders remain in their arrival order.

The temporary view contains pointers to the selected orders.

Changing the order of pointers in the view would not change the order of records in the original array.
